From 1a7f182cf10d6ff633ea00186534bffa208648be Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lars Wikman <lars@underjord.io>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 09:38:36 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] i2c: qup: don't leak a clock enable on resume while runtime
 suspended

qup_i2c_suspend() leaves the clocks alone when the controller is already
runtime suspended, but qup_i2c_resume() enables them unconditionally.
The device stays runtime suspended, so nothing disables them again: each
system suspend taken while the bus is idle leaves the core and iface
clocks enabled once more, and from the first one on they never turn off.

Only enable the clocks on resume when suspend disabled them.

Signed-off-by: Lars Wikman <lars@underjord.io>
---
 drivers/i2c/busses/i2c-qup.c | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/i2c/busses/i2c-qup.c b/drivers/i2c/busses/i2c-qup.c
index a0e076f..6aa16d1 100644
--- a/drivers/i2c/busses/i2c-qup.c
+++ b/drivers/i2c/busses/i2c-qup.c
@@ -1988,6 +1988,10 @@ static int qup_i2c_suspend(struct device *device)
 
 static int qup_i2c_resume(struct device *device)
 {
+	/* Suspend only turned the clocks off if runtime PM had them on. */
+	if (pm_runtime_suspended(device))
+		return 0;
+
 	qup_i2c_pm_resume_runtime(device);
 	pm_request_autosuspend(device);
 	return 0;
-- 
